; Bitmap address of a cell from its pixel row and byte column
;
; Converts a position given as a pixel row L and a byte column H into the address of that byte in the screen bitmap.
; Only correct when L is a multiple of 8, the top pixel line of a character cell: the low three bits of L would reach
; the high byte twice (observed: L = 1 gives $6100 instead of $4100). Used by #R$9F94 only, whose operands are
; cell-aligned.
; .
; Hardware: knows the layout of the screen bitmap at $4000-$57FF.
;
; L Pixel row, a multiple of 8
; H Byte column 0-31
; O:HL Bitmap address
@label=BitmapAddress
c$A1DE LD A,L        ;
 $A1DF ADD A,A       ;
 $A1E0 ADD A,A       ;
 $A1E1 AND $E0       ;
 $A1E3 ADD A,H       ;
 $A1E4 LD H,A        ;
 $A1E5 LD A,L        ;
 $A1E6 RRCA          ;
 $A1E7 RRCA          ;
 $A1E8 RRCA          ;
 $A1E9 XOR L         ;
 $A1EA AND $F8       ;
 $A1EC XOR L         ;
@isub=OR SCREEN_HIGH
 $A1ED OR $40        ;
 $A1EF LD L,H        ;
 $A1F0 LD H,A        ;
 $A1F1 RET           ;
